# Dependencies
node_modules

# Frontend build output and inputs.
#
# NOTE the `frontend/` prefix — it is load-bearing. A bare `dist` rule would also
# match backend/internal/dist, and git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded
# directory, which would make the committed //go:embed placeholder below
# impossible to track.
frontend/dist
frontend/dist.zip
_source
.vite

# NOTE: frontend/kb-corpus.txt is deliberately NOT ignored, though it is generated
# output. It is the entire text a public-facing insurance assistant answers from, so
# it needs to be reviewable and diffable in a pull request — a wrong line in there
# reaches customers. Regenerate with frontend/scripts/export-kb.mjs and commit the
# result alongside the copy change that caused it.

# Backend build output and secrets.
backend/bin
.env
.env.local

# The real Vite output is overlaid here by the Docker build; only the placeholder
# index.html is tracked, so //go:embed compiles from a clean checkout. The `/*`
# excludes the directory's *contents* rather than the directory, which is what lets
# the negation below work at all.
backend/internal/dist/*
!backend/internal/dist/index.html

# go.sum is deliberately NOT ignored — the Railway build runs `go mod download` and
# fails module verification without it.
